---

Checkpoint types

Checkpoint| Meaning
"base.pt"| Starting checkpoint of the training run
"best.pt"| Best checkpoint based on validation loss
"live.pt"| Latest checkpoint that can continue training
"history/"| Old checkpoints kept as backups

Lower validation loss = better checkpoint.

---

Add checkpoint as BEST

RUN

python scripts\checkpoints.py save FILE.pt --as best --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

Example:

python scripts\checkpoints.py save checkpoints\ored_v2\best.pt --as best --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

"best.pt" replaces the current best only when the new checkpoint has a better validation result.

To force replacement:

python scripts\checkpoints.py save FILE.pt --as best --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --force

The old "best.pt" is kept in "history/".

---

Add checkpoint as LIVE

RUN

python scripts\checkpoints.py save FILE.pt --as live --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

Example:

python scripts\checkpoints.py save checkpoints\ored_v2\live.pt --as live --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

"live.pt" must contain everything needed to continue training.

If it does not contain the required training state, use "--init-from" instead.

---

Add checkpoint to HISTORY

RUN

python scripts\checkpoints.py save FILE.pt --as history --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

Example:

python scripts\checkpoints.py save checkpoints\ored_v2\best.pt --as history --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

This keeps the checkpoint as a backup in "history/".

---

Add checkpoint as BASE

"base.pt" is created automatically when a new training run starts.

You normally do not add "base.pt" manually.

To start a new training run from an existing checkpoint:

python scripts\train.py --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --set run_name=ored_v2 --init-from checkpoints\char_transformer_v2\best.pt --set training.epochs=40 --set training.device=cuda

The existing checkpoint is used as the starting weights and the new run creates its own "base.pt".

---

Train

RUN

python scripts\generate_facts.py --repeats 20
python scripts\train.py --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --set run_name=ored_v2 --set training.epochs=40 --set training.device=cuda

During training:

base.pt
   ↓
live.pt
   ↓
validation
   ↓
better? ── yes ──→ best.pt
   │
   no
   ↓
best.pt stays the same

Old replaced checkpoints are kept in:

history/

---

Start training from another checkpoint

python scripts\train.py --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --set run_name=ored_v2 --init-from checkpoints\char_transformer_v2\best.pt --set training.epochs=40 --set training.device=cuda

"--init-from" = start a new run using another checkpoint's weights.

---

Continue stopped training

python scripts\train.py --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --resume-live --set training.epochs=40

"--resume-live" = continue training from "live.pt".

---

Merge LIVE into BEST

After an online-learning session creates "live.pt":

RUN

python scripts\checkpoints.py merge-live --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

It compares "live.pt" and "best.pt" using the same validation data.

If LIVE is better

live.pt
   ↓
best.pt

old best.pt
   ↓
history/

If LIVE is not better

best.pt stays unchanged

Example:

live = 3.07018
best = 3.37613

Because lower validation loss is better:

3.07018 < 3.37613

So "live.pt" becomes "best.pt".

